 ## Overview
-The AnySplat Pipeline is a feed-forward method for reconstructing 3D scenes from uncalibrated, unconstrained image collections by directly predicting 3D Gaussian primitives and camera poses [S1, unofficial]. It differs from iterative optimization-based Gaussian Splatting by using a transformer-based encoder-decoder to infer scene parameters in a single forward pass, and from other generalizable methods by explicitly predicting camera poses alongside geometry to handle uncalibrated inputs [S1, unofficial].
+AnySplat is a feed-forward, generalizable reconstruction method that predicts a set of 3D Gaussians directly from uncalibrated input images, eliminating the need for per-scene optimization [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods by predicting camera poses and depth maps alongside Gaussian parameters, using pseudo-geometry priors from a pretrained Vision Transformer (VGGT) to supervise the geometry, thereby enabling robust reconstruction from unconstrained, uncalibrated views [S1, unofficial].
 
